While that builds, I found a real problem in my own setup. The generated meshes wind counter-clockwise as seen from outside, but both backends currently treat clockwise-on-screen as front, so every one-sided quad facing the camera would be culled. I'm switching both backends to counter-clockwise front faces, which is the glTF convention. DX12 gets `FrontCounterClockwise`, and Vulkan gets `VK_FRONT_FACE_CLOCKWISE`, which matches because its y-down framebuffer reverses the sign.
