I've found both remaining mismatches, and both are real. The first is a sign error in my tangent frame. The cross-product form I used gives T = −X where the U axis runs along +X, so the normal map tilts the wrong way on both backends. I'll switch to the explicit solve for the tangent and bitangent, which gives exactly dP/du and dP/dv. The second is quantization in the 32×32 BRDF table. A nearest-texel lookup jumps between entries when a pixel's `n·v` crosses a texel boundary, which explains the 4-level differences. I'll make the table lookup bilinear in both the shader and the CPU reference.
